# Keep the knowledge graph to this project's own code.
#
# Without this, 46% of the graph (442 of 963 nodes) was agent skill documentation rather
# than nuvaiq source — and indexed twice over, since .agents/skills and .claude/skills are
# the same 11 react-three-fiber SKILL.md files reached through a symlink. The practical
# effect was that a query like "where is the cursor spotlight glow defined" came back with
# fifty nodes of R3F lighting/post-processing docs and nothing from src/ at all, spending
# its whole token budget on noise. Those docs are reference material for the agent to read
# directly when needed; they are not part of this codebase's structure and do not belong
# in a graph used to navigate it.
.agents/
.claude/

# Derived output — indexing the graph's own report back into the graph.
graphify-out/
dist/

# A bundled build artifact that lives at the root rather than inside dist/, so the line above
# does not catch it. At 8.8MB it is by far the largest file in the repo and it is entirely
# generated: every dependency the app pulls in, flattened into one file. Indexed, it swamps the
# graph with node_modules internals — a query for "which components use RevealLight" came back
# led by motion-dom projection helpers and the sandbox's demo functions, because those exist in
# here hundreds of times over. Nothing in it is a source of truth about this codebase.
dist-eager-probe.js
